    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No 4 Exham Place is located in a quiet city centre location just off George’s Quay and minutes’ walk to the South Mall, Patrick Street, MTU Crawford Art College and U.C.C. and has all the amenities city centre living has to offer.\r\n\r\nConstructed in mid 1990’s the property is part of a development of townhouses in Cork City’s South Parish with a lovely community and St Finbarr’s Church on Dunbar Street dating back to 1766. It is close to Douglas Street and George’s Quay, the Nano Nagle Centre, bars, restaurants and more. \r\n\r\nEntering the hallway terracotta tiling runs through the ground floor giving a spacious feel.  The kitchen to the front has shaker-style fitted units and dining, this opens by double doors to the living room which in turn opens via sliding glass doors to the rear yard.  The rear yard with some planting already in place and has the potential to be a beautiful space enhancing both indoor and outdoor living. There is a rear pedestrian entrance. \r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\nGround Floor: Hallway, Kitchen, Living Room, Guest W.C.\r\nFirst Floor: 3 Bedrooms Bathroom.\r\nFloor Area: 77m2 \r\nSee Floor plans for details.\r\n\r\nThis 3-bedroom house is in walk-in condition and viewing is recommended.\r\n\r\nServices: Mains Water & Drainage, Electricity, Gas Fired Central Heating.\r\nBER: D 101394013\r\n\r\nThis property will appeal to private buyers and investors."
      },
